& [ShapeProof] is one closed sum
  + [open_fault] has exact common identity plus nonzero error
  + [query_fault] adds exactly one of four closed query stages plus nonzero error
  + [complete] requires strong identity, canonical volume-GUID path, complete volume and remote records, and one disposition
  + [partial_evidence] is structurally absent from both fault variants
  + [unknown_field_variant_or_missing_value] rejects during strict decoding

& [PathProof] is lexical
  + [accepted] is canonical uppercase extended-DOS drive root and descendant syntax
  + [rejected] is relative, ordinary DOS, lowercase drive, drive-relative, UNC, volume-GUID input, device-shaped, forward slash, NUL, repeated separator, dot, dot-dot, trailing descendant separator, and resource excess
  + [existence_query] is zero
  + [final_path] reuses the exact proven TopologyReceipt 0.2 volume-GUID validator

& [CompleteEvidenceProof] is bounded
  + [identity] reuses 64-bit volume serial plus canonical lowercase 128-bit file identity
  + [volume] admits empty or bounded NUL-free volume name, u32 serial and flags, component length 1 through 32767, and nonblank ASCII filesystem name through 64 bytes
  + [remote] admits structure version 1 or 2, u16 structure size exactly 116, u32 protocol, three u16 protocol-version fields, and u32 flags
  + [reserved_remote_fields] reject as unknown JSON
  + [serial_equivalence_claim] is absent

& [DispositionProof] is exhaustive
  + [eligible_local_ntfs] passes only for protocol zero and exact NTFS
  + [reject_remote_protocol] passes only for nonzero protocol regardless of filesystem
  + [reject_unsupported_file_system] passes only for protocol zero and non-NTFS
  + [truth_table] exercises all three supplied dispositions over local NTFS, local ReFS, remote NTFS, and remote ReFS
  + [contradictory_pair] rejects
  + [protocol_zero] remains explicitly invalidatable by target-host evidence or stronger primary documentation

